*.swpBentley-Ottmann Line Sweep (Segment Intersection)Core Idea: An output-sensitive sweep-line framework that efficiently locates all intersection points within a massive set of line segments without running all pairwise checks.Mechanism: An imaginary scanline sweeps uniformly across the plane. The algorithm relies on two data structures: an Event Queue $Q$ (storing segment endpoints and discovered intersections sorted lexicographically) and a Sweep Line Status tree $T$ (a balanced search tree keeping track of the vertical order of segments currently intersecting the scanline). Crucially, segments can only intersect if they become immediate neighbors in $T$. Whenever segment adjacencies change (upon segment insertion, removal, or crossing events), neighbors are checked for intersections, and any newly discovered intersection points are inserted as future events into $Q$.Complexity: $O((n + k) \log n)$ time complexity, where $k$ represents the total number of actual intersections found; $O(n + k)$ space complexity.Bentley-Ottmann Line Sweep (Segment Intersection)Core Idea: An output-sensitive sweep-line framework that efficiently locates all intersection points within a massive set of line segments without running all pairwise checks.Mechanism: An imaginary scanline sweeps uniformly across the plane. The algorithm relies on two data structures: an Event Queue $Q$ (storing segment endpoints and discovered intersections sorted lexicographically) and a Sweep Line Status tree $T$ (a balanced search tree keeping track of the vertical order of segments currently intersecting the scanline). Crucially, segments can only intersect if they become immediate neighbors in $T$. Whenever segment adjacencies change (upon segment insertion, removal, or crossing events), neighbors are checked for intersections, and any newly discovered intersection points are inserted as future events into $Q$.Complexity: $O((n + k) \log n)$ time complexity, where $k$ represents the total number of actual intersections found; $O(n + k)$ space complexity.
